      cmd         : "/bin/grep -r '^[^#].*!authenticate' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/ | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\" ; else print \"fail\"}'"
      expect      : "^pass$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "5.2.8 Ensure sudo pwfeedback is configured"
      info        : "The pwfeedback option provides visual feedback (for example, an asterisk) for each character as the sudo password is typed. When not enabled (the default), no feedback is displayed.

Visual feedback discloses the exact length of the password to anyone able to observe the terminal or a session recording, weakening it against shoulder-surfing and offline analysis. The option has also been associated with input-handling defects in older versions of sudo. Leaving pwfeedback disabled removes the length side-channel and keeps sudo on its hardened default."
      solution    : "Ensure sudo does not display feedback while the password is typed. Edit the appropriate sudoers file with visudo and remove any line that enables pwfeedback, or explicitly disable it:

# visudo

Add or correct the line:

Defaults !pwfeedback"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.5,800-171|3.1.6,800-171|3.5.11,800-171r3|03.01.06a.,800-171r3|03.01.06b.,800-171r3|03.05.11,800-53|AC-6(2),800-53|AC-6(5),800-53|IA-6,800-53r5|IA-6,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CSCv7|4.3,CSCv8|5.4,CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.2.3,ITSG-33|AC-6(2),ITSG-33|AC-6(5),ITSG-33|IA-6,ITSG-33|IA-6a.,LEVEL|1A,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.5.1,NESA|T5.6.1,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|AM32,NIAv2|AM33,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,NIAv2|VL3a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|1.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27892"
      cmd         : "/bin/grep -rPi -- '^\\h*Defaults\\h+([^#]+,\\h*)?pwfeedback\\b' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/ | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\" ; else print \"fail\"}'"
      expect      : "^pass$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "5.2.9 Ensure sudo visiblepw is configured"
      info        : "The visiblepw sudo option controls whether sudo will prompt for a password on a terminal that cannot disable local echo. When not enabled (the default), sudo refuses to run rather than prompt for a password that would be displayed as it is typed.

If visiblepw is enabled, sudo prompts for a password even when the terminal cannot suppress echo (for example, a command run over SSH without a pseudo-terminal). The password is then entered in cleartext where it can be observed, captured in a screen or session recording, or written to logs. Leaving visiblepw disabled ensures a password is only requested when it can be entered without being displayed."
      solution    : "Ensure sudo will not prompt for a password on a terminal where it would be displayed. Edit the appropriate sudoers file with visudo and remove any line that enables visiblepw, or explicitly disable it:

# visudo

Add or correct the line:

Defaults !visiblepw

Impact:

Automated or non-interactive workflows that invoke sudo without a pseudo-terminal will fail with a password-prompt error rather than exposing the password. Allocate a pseudo-terminal (for example, ssh -t ) for such workflows, or use an appropriate documented exception."
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.5,800-171|3.1.6,800-171|3.5.11,800-171r3|03.01.06a.,800-171r3|03.01.06b.,800-171r3|03.05.11,800-53|AC-6(2),800-53|AC-6(5),800-53|IA-6,800-53r5|IA-6,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CSCv7|4.3,CSCv8|5.4,CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.2.3,ITSG-33|AC-6(2),ITSG-33|AC-6(5),ITSG-33|IA-6,ITSG-33|IA-6a.,LEVEL|1A,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.5.1,NESA|T5.6.1,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|AM32,NIAv2|AM33,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,NIAv2|VL3a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|1.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27892"
      cmd         : "/bin/grep -rPi -- '^\\h*Defaults\\h+([^#]+,\\h*)?visiblepw\\b' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/ 2>/dev/null | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\" ; else print \"fail\"}'"
      expect      : "^pass$"
