      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "5.4.2.2 Ensure root is the only GID 0 account"
      info        : "An account's primary group is identified by the group ID (GID) in its /etc/passwd entry. GID 0 is the root group, which the root account uses as its primary group by default.

Using GID 0 for the root account helps prevent root -owned files from accidentally becoming accessible to non-privileged users."
      solution    : "Run the following command to reassign any account other than root that has primary GID 0 to an appropriate group:

# usermod -g <NEW_GID> <username>

