      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "5.4.2.3 Ensure group root is the only GID 0 group"
      info        : "Groups are defined in /etc/group, each identified by a group ID (GID). GID 0 is reserved for the root group, the privileged group associated with the superuser.

If a group other than root is assigned GID 0, it silently shares the privileges of the root group. Such a duplicate is easy to overlook and undermines accountability for access granted through the root group."
