        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "6.1.1.2 Ensure systemd-journal-remote is not in use"
          info        : "The systemd-journal-remote package provides the ability to receive journal log entries from remote hosts over the network, which makes the receiving host a log server. The same package supplies both the sending and the receiving functions; the receiving side is handled by two units, systemd-journal-remote.socket and systemd-journal-remote.service.

If a client is configured to also receive log data, thus turning it into a log server, the client system is acting outside its operational boundary. Disabling the systemd-journal-remote receiver is collector hygiene that applies regardless of whether rsyslog or journald is the primary log path."
          solution    : "Run the following commands to stop and mask systemd-journal-remote.socket and systemd-journal-remote.service:

# systemctl stop systemd-journal-remote.socket systemd-journal-remote.service
# systemctl mask systemd-journal-remote.socket systemd-journal-remote.service"
