Persistent, reliable logging is fundamental to security operations: it preserves the record of system and security events needed for accountability, threat detection, incident investigation, and forensic analysis. The systemd journal stores its logs in volatile memory by default, so without a persistent logging service those records can be lost across a reboot or under memory pressure. Installing rsyslog establishes durable on-disk log retention and the foundation for later centralization and protection of that log data."
