      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27892"
      cmd         : "#!/bin/bash
  {
   a_conf=(/etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d/*.conf)
   while IFS= read -r l_inc; do
      for l_f in $l_inc; do
         [ -d \"$l_f\" ] && a_conf+=(\"$l_f\"/*.conf) || a_conf+=(\"$l_f\")
      done
   done < <(grep -Psoih -- '^\\h*(?:\\$IncludeConfig\\h+|include\\h*\\(\\h*file\\h*=\\h*\"?)\\K[^\")\\h]+' \"${a_conf[@]}\" 2>/dev/null)
   grep -Psi -- '^\\h*module\\(load=\"?(imtcp|imudp|imptcp|imrelp)\"?\\)' \"${a_conf[@]}\" 2>/dev/null
   grep -Psi -- '^\\h*input\\(type=\"?(imtcp|imudp|imptcp|imrelp)\"?' \"${a_conf[@]}\" 2>/dev/null
   grep -Psi -- '^\\h*\\$ModLoad\\h+(imtcp|imudp|imptcp|imrelp)\\b' \"${a_conf[@]}\" 2>/dev/null
   grep -Psi -- '^\\h*\\$(InputTCPServerRun|UDPServerRun|InputPTCPServerRun|InputRELPServerRun)\\b' \"${a_conf[@]}\" 2>/dev/null
} | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\" ; else print \"fail\"}'"
      expect      : "^pass$"
      severity    : MEDIUM
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "6.1.2.8 Ensure rsyslog logging rules are configured"
      info        : "The /etc/rsyslog.conf file and the drop-in files ending in .conf under /etc/rsyslog.d/ specify rsyslog's logging rules - which classes of messages (by facility and severity) are recorded and which files they are written to.

Security-relevant events - such as authentication successes and failures, privilege escalation, and root activity - are recorded through rsyslog. If logging rules are not configured to capture and retain these events, the records needed for accountability, detection, and investigation may never be written.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "- Edit the following lines in the /etc/rsyslog.conf and /etc/rsyslog.d/*.conf files as appropriate for your environment.

Note: The below configuration is shown for example purposes only. Due care should be given to how the organization wishes to store log data.

*.emerg :omusrmsg:*
auth,authpriv.* /var/log/secure
mail.* -/var/log/mail
mail.info -/var/log/mail.info
mail.warning -/var/log/mail.warn
mail.err /var/log/mail.err
cron.* /var/log/cron
*.=warning;*.=err -/var/log/warn
*.crit /var/log/warn
*.*;mail.none;news.none -/var/log/messages
local0,local1.* -/var/log/localmessages
local2,local3.* -/var/log/localmessages
local4,local5.* -/var/log/localmessages
local6,local7.* -/var/log/localmessages

 - Run the following command to restart rsyslog :

# systemctl restart rsyslog"
