    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"OR">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "AIDE integrity check scheduled via cron"
          cmd         : "/bin/grep -rEi 'aide[[:space:]]+(--check|--update)' /var/spool/cron/ /etc/crontab /etc/cron.d /etc/cron.hourly /etc/cron.daily /etc/cron.weekly /etc/cron.monthly 2>/dev/null | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"fail\"; else print \"pass\"}'"
          expect      : "^pass$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "AIDE integrity check scheduled via enabled or active systemd timer"
          cmd         : "#!/bin/bash
  {
     for t in $(systemctl list-unit-files --type=timer --no-legend | awk '{print $1}'); do
        en=\"$(systemctl is-enabled \"$t\" 2>/dev/null)\"; ac=\"$(systemctl is-active \"$t\" 2>/dev/null)\"
        [ \"$en\" = \"enabled\" ] || [ \"$ac\" = \"active\" ] || continue
        s=\"$(systemctl show -p Unit --value \"$t\")\"; [ -z \"$s\" ] && s=\"${t%.timer}.service\"
        systemctl cat \"$s\" 2>/dev/null | grep -Eq 'ExecStart=.*aide[[:space:]]+(--check|--update)' && echo \"$t -> $s\"
     done
  } | /bin/awk '{ print } END { if (NR != 0) print \"pass\" }'"
          expect      : "^pass$"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "6.3.2 Ensure filesystem integrity is regularly checked"
          info        : "Periodic checking of filesystem integrity detects unauthorized changes to files. AIDE (Advanced Intrusion Detection Environment) compares the current state of the filesystem against a previously initialized baseline database; this recommendation ensures that comparison runs automatically on a regular schedule rather than only on demand.

Periodic file checking allows the system administrator to determine on a regular basis if critical files have been changed in an unauthorized fashion. Running the integrity check on a defined schedule -- rather than manually or ad hoc -- ensures changes are detected consistently and reduces the window in which unauthorized modifications can go unnoticed."
          solution    : "Configure a systemd timer to run a periodic AIDE integrity check.

 - Create the file /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.service with the following content:

[Unit]
Description=Aide Check

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/sbin/aide --check

 - Create the file /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.timer with the following content:

[Unit]
Description=Aide check every day at 5AM

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 05:00:00
Persistent=true
Unit=aidecheck.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target

 - Run the following commands to set access on the unit files, reload systemd, and enable the timer:

# chown root:root /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.service /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.timer
# chmod 0644 /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.service /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.timer
# systemctl daemon-reload
# systemctl enable --now aidecheck.timer

Impact:

Scheduled integrity checks consume CPU and I/O when they run; choose a schedule and time that balance timely detection against system load."
          reference   : "800-171|3.1.7,800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-171r3|03.01.07b.,800-171r3|03.03.01,800-171r3|03.03.03,800-53|AC-6(9),800-53|AU-2,800-53|AU-12,800-53|SI-7,800-53r5|SI-7,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(a),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CSCv7|14.9,CSCv8|3.14,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF|DE.CM-7,CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF|PR.DS-6,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|DE.CM-03,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|ID.RA-09,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,CSF2.0|PR.DS-01,CSF2.0|PR.DS-02,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.PS-02,CSF2.0|PR.PS-04,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),HIPAA|164.312(c)(1),HIPAA|164.312(c)(2),HIPAA|164.312(e)(2)(i),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.4.3,ITSG-33|AC-6,ITSG-33|AU-2,ITSG-33|AU-12,ITSG-33|SI-7,ITSG-33|SI-7a.,LEVEL|1A,NESA|M1.2.2,NESA|M5.5.1,NESA|T3.4.1,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T7.3.2,NESA|T7.3.3,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM7,NIAv2|AM11a,NIAv2|AM11b,NIAv2|AM11c,NIAv2|AM11d,NIAv2|AM11e,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,NIAv2|SS30,NIAv2|VL8,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.5.5,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3"
